-- title:
--   A cubic-switch candidate exists at every permitted reporting level
-- statement:
--   Let $h,J,k\in\mathbb N$ satisfy $k\le\lfloor13J/20\rfloor$, and put $r=2h(J-k)$, the residual subset size at level $k$. There exists a natural switch index $q\le\lfloor r/2\rfloor$ such that
--
--   $$
--   (291J+1000k)r^3
--   \le10(J-k)\bigl(799qr^2+72q^2r+24q^3\bigr).
--   $$
--
--   Equivalently, the explicitly enumerated finite candidate set for this residual size is nonempty. The statement includes vanishing residual size, in particular the cases $h=0$ or $J=0$.
--
--   It ensures that selecting the minimum accepted switch index is justified throughout the reporting hierarchy's executable depth range.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/SharedReportingBankLevels.lean#L30-L44

